{"id": "EUVD-2026-64371", "enisaUuid": "f8752d2d-38fe-309b-8a10-36c5a175979f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: tap: set skb->dev before parsing virtio net header in tap_get_user_xdp()\n\nThe commit 4f61f133f354 (\"net: tap: NULL pointer derefence in\ndev_parse_header_protocol when skb->dev is null\") fixed a crash in\ntap_get_user() by assigning skb->dev before calling tun_vnet_hdr_to_skb().\nThis is required because virtio_net_hdr_to_skb() may invoke\ndev_parse_header_protocol(), which dereferences skb->dev. Without the\nassignment, a NULL pointer dereference can occur.\n\nHowever, tap_get_user_xdp() still parses the virtio-net header before\nassigning skb->dev. When the vhost TX path passes an XDP buffer containing\na GSO virtio-net header but the protocol is set to zero on purpose,\ntun_vnet_hdr_to_skb() can reach dev_parse_header_protocol() while skb->dev\nis still NULL, resulting in a crash.\n\nFix this by looking up the tap device and assigning skb->dev before calling\ntun_vnet_hdr_to_skb(), matching the ordering already used in\ntap_get_user(). Preserve the existing RCU read-side critical section across\ndev_queue_xmit().", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:32:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:07", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61dd022c55c7307ec119e5672cb141cccbecf3b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15583b07fd691a844fbf7b3ad612cdc9e9a657c0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b444b126cd8e4473e652f529753ed4dd1360a9c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/164c31ee252ebd1ac8f44c2dfc5486b6d9a0379b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3874892dd27d5387aa9a06f58d9060f18f351d24"], "aliases": ["GHSA-23q4-679m-qgxw", "CVE-2026-74684"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "088f8a14-c430-3f0e-af3a-915d930f7a59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.106 <5.5"}, {"id": "106b0267-d73a-3bf9-9abc-32108a6df175", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "1f4bf309-cdaa-338f-8631-93519afa86b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.24 <5.11"}, {"id": "36d2a9eb-b9d3-3576-b2ef-2d42aba284fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "faa3baa2828c5e1c4374f3e60041f75c64f5fcb6"}, {"id": "3d3edba4-2853-39c9-a9de-0354cb3c0582", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "924a9bc362a5223cd448ca08c3dde21235adc310 <15583b07fd691a844fbf7b3ad612cdc9e9a657c0"}, {"id": "4301d1e6-f9c1-3759-a0f8-c6bfc22b412f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.45"}, {"id": "46da9aaa-af87-353e-8bab-3d98b73841bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4aba22b7-7ef5-3273-8027-a31a843c4644", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "924a9bc362a5223cd448ca08c3dde21235adc310 <8b444b126cd8e4473e652f529753ed4dd1360a9c"}, {"id": "50b0f914-d09c-399e-b768-2638e6a7b1f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.14.226 <4.15"}, {"id": "56965ecb-5fb6-3f13-9bc7-a7158d486fee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "924a9bc362a5223cd448ca08c3dde21235adc310 <164c31ee252ebd1ac8f44c2dfc5486b6d9a0379b"}, {"id": "5acb8a73-adb0-3ad8-ac02-88b90657dbae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "99b1d3f74b9ef72c2f74c8e4c078e1bc0706e748"}, {"id": "6433abc8-0518-30d7-83fd-e806baaa9a43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11.7 <5.12"}, {"id": "77cb354b-d635-3d0e-9e5e-9452dbba2a85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version":